out thousands of people this  is not the largest caravan today but  it's certainly uh the largest one that  we've seen so far this year um what  we're also hearing from people is that  regardless of whether or not they are  able to receive their transit visas  today or tomorrow they're going to  continue to walk  we spoke to an elderly woman in her 70s  from nicaragua who  told us that she's tired of waiting she  doesn't want to wait for a transit visa  she's going to go it on her own this is  something that is  not recommended for migrants traveling  the sense is that it's better to travel  as a group they run many many risks on  their way to the northern border and  everyone here is saying that they are  committed to reaching the u.s southern  border  algae sirius manuel rappelo reporting  live there from southern mexico and many  thanks indeed
 

